---
id: org.dxos.spec.session
name: DSL.Session
version: 1.0
extends:
  - org.dxos.spec.changelog
---

The session dialect. A `SESSION.mdl` is an agent's record of one working session, kept for the person who reads it
instead of the chat: the questions only they can answer, the goals and their state, the pull requests, and an
append-only timeline. The status-board skill renders it as a page.

A session file is a log, not a spec, so the changelog dialect's rule 1 (every change adds a decision) does not apply
to it. Its questions and their answers are the changelog dialect's `question` and `decision`, and stay append-only.

## Extensions

| Term    | URI                       |
| ------- | ------------------------- |
| `goal`  | `org.dxos.mdl.goal@1.0`  |
| `pr`    | `org.dxos.mdl.pr@1.0`    |
| `event` | `org.dxos.mdl.event@1.0` |

## Document

The frontmatter `name` is the page title. The first paragraph after the `#` heading is the one-line summary.
Sections, in this order:

| Section             | Blocks                                             |
| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| `## Questions`      | `question Q-n`                                     |
| `## Goals`          | `goal G-n`                                         |
| `## Pull requests`  | `pr PR-n`                                          |
| `## Changelog`      | `decision D-n`, each answering a question          |
| `## Timeline`       | `event T-n`, oldest first                          |

## Rules

1. **Terse.** A block's title has 12 words or fewer; a `notes` item has 25 or fewer, and a block has at most 6.
2. **A question is open until a decision answers it.** A goal whose `blockedBy` names an open question renders as
   blocked, whatever its `status`.
3. **The timeline is append-only.** An event is never edited or removed, ids are monotonic (`T-1`, `T-2`, …), and dates
   never go backwards.

## Definitions

```mdl
ext goal
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.goal@1.0
  desc: |
    One outcome the session works toward. The title says what is true for the reader when it is done ("The page
    renders dark."), not the work that gets it there.
  fields:
    status: todo | backlog | started | review | done | duplicate | blocked | cancelled | failed
    blockedBy?: RefList         # questions the goal waits on, e.g. [Q-1]
    notes?: ProseList           # the details the page shows when the goal is opened
  links:
    blockedBy: depends-on
  role: anchor
  icon: ph--target--regular
```

```mdl
ext pr
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.pr@1.0
  desc: A pull request the session opened or drives. The title is the PR's effect, in one line.
  fields:
    ref: Identifier             # owner/repo#number
    status: draft | open | failing | landing | queued | merged | closed
    branch?: Identifier         # the head branch
    goals?: RefList             # the goals the PR serves
    notes?: ProseList
  links:
    goals: implements
  role: structure
  icon: ph--git-pull-request--regular
```

`landing` means the `land` skill drives the PR: it fixes CI and keeps the branch current until the merge queue takes
it (`queued`).

```mdl
ext event
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.event@1.0
  desc: One thing that happened in the session, as one line. Events are appended, never edited.
  fields:
    date: DateTime              # ISO 8601, to the minute, UTC
    by?: ActorRef               # user:<handle> | agent:<name>
    refs?: RefList              # the blocks it concerns
  links:
    refs: references
  role: context
  icon: ph--clock--regular
```

## Example

```mdl
goal G-1: The page renders dark.
  status: started
  blockedBy: [Q-1]
  notes:
    - The Artifact frame pins a light color scheme.
```

```mdl
pr PR-1: Build the status board from mdl.
  ref: dxos/dxos#14647
  branch: claude/status-board
  status: landing
  goals: [G-1]
```

```mdl
event T-1: Opened [PR-1] as a draft.
  date: 2026-11-21T11:55Z
  by: agent:claude-code
```
